  "managerGates": {
    "_doc": "Channel-desk manager capability gates (#289+, docs/planning/manager-roles-channel-desk.md §3). Each acting capability earns a hard threshold on its own skill axis (0–100). M2 (#289) consumes pricing: top UCM pricing >= threshold unlocks the standing auto-pricing policy; below = suggestion-only. M3 (#290) consumes t_o_closing: top UCM t_o_closing >= threshold lets the UCM desk ALL below-floor discounts; below = the understaffed path (rare rate-gated escalation, the rest walk). M4 adds condition_reading. Placeholder magnitudes — calibrated in the S14 pass (#286). Green UCM ~50, seasoned ~72–82, so 60 sits each gate as an earned mid-career step.",
    "actThresholds": {
      "pricing": 60,
      "t_o_closing": 60
    }
  },
  "tradePolicy": {
    "_doc": "Per-slot trade-acquisition policy (#172). The `multiplier` scales the staff's internal trade-in acceptance target (book × multiplier × read-confidence factor) inside DealEngine.evaluateTrade. Aggressive (>1) chases volume by paying over book — more trades acquired, thinner gross; Conservative (<1) protects gross by targeting under book — fewer trades, fatter margins; Market (1.0) appraises at honest book and is the default. The composition root resolves the selected id to its multiplier and threads it through the trade resolver; the setting persists per save slot. Retune the spread here without touching code.",
    "defaultId": "market",
    "policies": [
      {
        "id": "aggressive",
        "label": "Aggressive",
        "multiplier": 1.1,
        "blurb": "Pay up to 10% over book to win trades — more cars acquired, thinner gross per deal."
      },
      {
        "id": "market",
        "label": "Market",
        "multiplier": 1.0,
        "blurb": "Appraise trades at honest book value — balanced acquisition rate and gross."
      },
      {
        "id": "conservative",
        "label": "Conservative",
        "multiplier": 0.92,
        "blurb": "Target ~8% under book to protect gross — fewer trades acquired, fatter margins."
      }
    ]
  }
